{
  "id": 470324930,
  "iid": 24175,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ICMP: add expert warnings for malformed extension object lengths",
  "description": "ICMP extension object lengths are currently indicated only via appended\\\ntext such as \"Object with bad length\" or \"(truncated)\" in the protocol tree.\n\nThese malformed conditions are not surfaced through Expert Info, making\\\nthem harder to detect in analysis workflows and not directly filterable.\n\nAdd explicit Expert Info reporting for malformed ICMP extension object\\\nlengths in dissect_icmp_extension():\n\n* Invalid object lengths (\\< 4), flagged as PI_MALFORMED/PI_ERROR\n* Truncated objects where declared length exceeds available data,\\\n  flagged as PI_MALFORMED/PI_WARN\n\nThis improves visibility and filterability of malformed ICMP extension\\\nobjects.\n\nNo dissection logic is changed.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-04-03T13:49:08.069Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-05T21:09:18.177Z",
